# Named Dockerfile.dockerignore (not .dockerignore) so Docker picks this up
# from next to the Dockerfile it applies to, rather than looking for a
# .dockerignore at the build context root — which is the parent workspace
# directory shared by every sibling repo, not one we own or want to touch.
# Patterns below are evaluated relative to that context root regardless.
*
!gismo-agent-go
!gismo-agent-go/**
!gismo-sdk-go
!gismo-sdk-go/**
!gismo-contracts
!gismo-contracts/**
**/.git
**/.github
**/node_modules
